        {
          "source": "",
          "thread": "SEC political accountability",
          "why": "Gensler's contradictory signals, the fake social media post scandal, and Elizabeth Warren's pushback framed the SEC itself as a contested battleground, not just a neutral gatekeeper."
        },
        {
          "source": "",
          "thread": "Systemic and concentration risk",
          "why": "Concerns that ETF-driven demand concentrates BTC custody and ETH validator power in a handful of TradFi custodians attracted readers alert to the irony of decentralized assets being re-centralized through regulated wrappers."
        },
        {
          "source": "",
          "thread": "Altcoin ETF queue chaos",
          "why": "A 72-product backlog spanning XRP, Solana, Dogecoin, and Pudgy Penguins crystallized the absurdity and opportunity of the post-approval flood, drawing readers tracking which assets get legitimized next."
        },
        {
          "source": "",
          "thread": "Institutional VC capital rotation",
          "why": "Evidence that large investors chose Bitcoin ETFs over early-stage VC funding revealed ETFs as a competitive alternative asset class within crypto, not just a gateway product."
